---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/102896351/Agents';
---

<Base title="Contact" description="Report an error, suggest an agent, or send a pull request. AI Agents Hub is a one-developer open-source project.">
  <section class="hero" style="padding-top: 80px; padding-bottom: 24px;">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Contact</h1>
      <p>Want to add an agent, report a bug, or fix a stale number? The quickest route is a GitHub issue or pull request — email works too.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 640px;">
      <div class="contact-simple">
        <div class="contact-label">Contribute directly</div>
        <a class="contact-mail" href={REPO} target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/102896351/Agents</a>
        <p class="contact-hint">Every agent profile lives in <code>src/data/agents.ts</code> and the related data files. Fix a price, add a source link, or add a missing agent via an issue or pull request — the change history is public.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="contact-simple" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <div class="contact-label">Email</div>
        <a class="contact-mail" href="mailto:andynaonao@gmail.com">andynaonao@gmail.com</a>
        <p class="contact-hint">This is a one-person project, so there is no guaranteed reply time. For anything data-related, a public issue or pull request is faster and stays visible.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 48px;">
        <h2>When to reach out</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Missing an agent?</strong> Send the homepage / GitHub link, or open a pull request against the data file (usually faster).</li>
          <li><strong>Spotted stale info</strong> (star count, pricing, status, etc.)? Point it out with a source link and it will be corrected.</li>
          <li><strong>Business / partnership</strong> (brand collaboration, content syndication, API data partnerships).</li>
          <li><strong>Found a bug on the site itself</strong> (not a problem with any listed agent).</li>
          <li><strong>Have something to say</strong> — any thoughts, suggestions, or honest criticism about the AI agent space are welcome.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Submission checklist (new agent)</h2>
        <p>To make a listing easy to add, please include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Agent name + a one-line positioning</li>
          <li>Homepage / GitHub link</li>
          <li>License type (open source / commercial / freemium)</li>
          <li>One sentence on why it deserves a spot</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Pull requests are reviewed in the open. There is no promised turnaround,
          and this project does not guarantee that every suggestion will be published.
        </p>

        <h2>What we usually don't reply to</h2>
        <p>To keep the inbox usable, these are typically skipped:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>SEO link exchanges / bulk backlink requests</li>
          <li>Unsolicited "exclusive interview" or guest invitations</li>
          <li>Promotions unrelated to the AI agent topic</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If that sounds like your request, apologies in advance — and thanks for understanding.</p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Your email is used only for this conversation. It will not be added to any
          mailing list or shared with third parties. To delete previous correspondence,
          simply reply with "please delete my email." Full details are in the
          <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="verdict-box" style="margin-top: 24px;">
          <div class="label">About response times</div>
          <p style="margin: 0; color: var(--text);">
            This is a one-person side project. No response time is promised; public
            issues and pull requests on GitHub are the most reliable way to get a
            data correction merged.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
